    "title": "TDF nephrotoxicity with declining renal function",
    "message": "Guidelines state that if GFR is <60 mL/min on TDF, substitute with ABC. Patient's eGFR is 52 mL/min with creatinine steadily rising from 0.9 (2020) to 1.4 (2026), a clear worsening trend over 6 years. TDF is a known cause of chronic kidney disease and Fanconi syndrome. Urinalysis showing protein 1+ further supports TDF nephrotoxicity. Evidence against drug attribution: no back pain, no change in urine volume, stable weight, and no oedema. However, the progressive trajectory and proteinuria strongly suggest TDF contribution. Occasional ibuprofen use (2-3 times/week) may compound renal risk.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Substitute TDF with ABC per guidelines (GFR <60). Confirm ABC eligibility (HLA-B*5701 or clinical screening). Consider NSAID reduction to limit compounded renal injury.",
