    "title": "Fatigue may signal TDF toxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines list exhaustion or extreme fatigue, muscle cramps, and headache as presenting signs of TDF toxicity including lactic acidosis. Patient reports mild fatigue over 2 months. Evidence for drug attribution: TDF can cause fatigue via lactic acidosis or renal dysfunction, and eGFR is 52. Evidence against: fatigue is mild, patient attributes it to work schedule, no muscle cramps, headache, or abdominal pain reported, and Hb is 12.8 g/dL (not severely anaemic). Lactic acidosis typically presents acutely with severe symptoms. Non-drug causes remain plausible but renal decline warrants investigation.",
